// Phase 5C Task 2, design §3.4.3: butt caps on a two-point line, and a
// zero-length segment WITHIN a line. `plain` is a straight two-point line,
// 80 units long, thickness 12 -- the butt-cap reference. `repeated` is the
// same line in the same position with one extra point repeating the
// midpoint ((0,0),(40,0),(40,0),(80,0)), so it carries a genuine
// zero-length segment in its interior rather than at either end.
//
// Confirmed directly by calling pixi.js's own `buildLine` outside a
// browser on both point lists: the repeated point DOES produce NaN-valued
// vertices for the degenerate join geometry (dividing by a zero segment
// length), but every triangle touching a real (non-NaN) vertex reproduces
// the plain line's own rectangle exactly -- (0,+-6) through (80,+-6) --
// so the two fixtures are predicted to render pixel-identical, with the
// NaN triangles either discarded by the rasterizer or invisible regardless.
// `origin: (0, 0)` puts each line's pivot at its own first point (both
// point lists have bbox min (0,0)), so `position` names that point's own
// world coordinate.
scene {
  size: (280, 320)
  duration: 0.0333333333
  background: #000000

  line plain {
    position: (100, 100)
    origin: (0, 0)
    points: [(0, 0), (80, 0)]
    thickness: 12
    color: #ffffff
  }

  line repeated {
    position: (100, 220)
    origin: (0, 0)
    points: [(0, 0), (40, 0), (40, 0), (80, 0)]
    thickness: 12
    color: #ffffff
  }
}
